  "blurb": "Four go together. One does not. Find it.",
  "childIntro": "Look at all the pictures. Most of them belong in one group. One does not fit. Find the one that does not belong.",
  "howItWorks": "On OLSAT the pictures themselves are the answers: the child marks the one that does not belong. It appears only at levels A to C. The trick is that the odd one out is usually strongly connected to the group in some other way, so a child who follows their first association gets it wrong.",
  "parentTip": "Ask your child to name the group before naming the odd one out. Saying these are all things you play tells you far more than pointing. If the group name is vague, the answer will be a guess.",
